      "claim": "FIXED",
      "final_text": "I fixed the air steering in `travel` in `sim/src/mcsim/physics.py`. The visible suite (25 scenarios) and unit tests pass. I can't see the hidden holdouts, so I can't confirm they now pass.\n\n- **Cause:** while airborne, the sim used the ground acceleration formula with friction fixed at 1.0. That made mid-air steering much stronger than the real game's.\n- **Fix:** airborne acceleration is now the game's flat 0.02, or about 0.026 when sprinting. This part was already in the working-copy edit I found in `physics.py`.\n- **Why attempt 1 failed:** the sprinting value was computed in double precision, which is slightly off from the game's float arithmetic. A sprint jump drifted from the oracle by about 1e-7 in `z`, starting at tick 17. I now compute it as `f32(f32(0.02) + f32(0.02) * 0.3)`, and the same sprint-jump scenario matches the oracle exactly.\n\nI also checked a forward+left jump and a sprint jump where I release sprint and forward mid-air. Both match the oracle. I didn't save a repro.\n\nSTATUS: FIXED",
